  "description": "Weighted virtual tree; requires >>lca and publicly reuses _lca. Input is an undirected weighted forest on [base,n]; add(a,b,c=1) preserves edge costs and build(root=-1) rebuilds all components, processing the chosen root first. Do not bypass weighted input maintenance through _lca base mutators. make(keys) requires all supplied vertices to belong to one component; it returns the unique selected vertices plus their LCA closure in the current forward DFS order. Duplicates are removed; an empty input clears the virtual tree. There are no key-membership markers. nodes() returns a const reference to the cached virtual vertices; root() returns their virtual root, or -1 when empty. it_child(v,f) calls f(child,weight) for direct virtual children; it_edge(f) calls f(parent,child,weight) for all current virtual edges. make, build and clear invalidate previous virtual results; make reuses storage and clears only previously used virtual rows. Inherited parent(v) returns -1 at original component roots; inherited ret/ancestor/it/subtree queries describe the original forest, and inherited dist counts original edges. dist_root(v) returns the weighted distance from its component root; dist_tree(a,b) returns weighted path length, or -1 across components. Weighted prefixes and distance arithmetic use i128; all returned distances and compressed edge weights must fit ll. After input changes, build before any query or make. Constructor, clear and build are O(n log n); make is O(k_prev + k log k + k log n), where k_prev counts previous virtual vertices and k counts supplied keys. Cached nodes/root getters are O(1), child iteration is O(virtual outdegree), and edge iteration is O(current virtual vertices)."
